From 000b3cdfdeac10af680974a8612ce2e9b55d0a64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:36:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel material properties: symbols, shared kernel
 code

- the libraries export the name of the backend
  (`<name>_generic_parallel_backend`) and the version of the generated
  functions (`<name>_generic_parallel_api_version`), as for the
  behaviours. The version is the `MFRONT_GPMP_API_VERSION` macro of the new
  `MFront/GenericParallelMaterialProperty/MaterialProperty.h` header;
- the CUDA and HIP backends and the backends based on the C++ programming
  model share the beginning of the C functions (signature, checks of the
  arguments and of the strides), the body of the kernels, the selection
  of the kernel and the analysis of the results, written once in
  `BackendBase`. The two previous implementations had diverged (order of
  the checks, error messages, restoration of errno);
- the inclusion of the SYCL header is written by the SYCL backend only.

The tests of all the backends check the symbols of the backend and of the
version.
